WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.087
Telemetry quality determines whether collected data can support a decision.

00:00:05.087 --> 00:00:08.847
Completeness asks whether required activity is represented.

00:00:08.847 --> 00:00:13.050
Accuracy asks whether fields describe the correct event.

00:00:13.050 --> 00:00:20.349
Reliable asset mapping, units, identities, protocol decoding, and status values are all part of quality.

00:00:20.349 --> 00:00:23.667
Time synchronization is essential for correlation.

00:00:23.667 --> 00:00:30.524
Controllers, servers, remote sites, and security platforms may use different clocks or time zones.

00:00:30.524 --> 00:00:38.707
Record clock sources, expected drift, and timestamp meaning so investigators can build a defensible sequence of events.

00:00:38.707 --> 00:00:45.564
Retention should reflect investigation needs, source volume, operational cycles, legal constraints, and storage cost.

00:00:45.564 --> 00:00:51.536
Normalization makes data searchable across systems, but it must preserve source detail.

00:00:51.536 --> 00:00:57.508
Overly broad parsing can hide important industrial fields or produce misleading values.

00:00:57.508 --> 00:01:03.480
Coverage is the portion of important activity that the program can observe.

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:12.106
Gaps may include serial networks, encrypted sessions, dormant assets, unsupported devices, local engineering actions, or sites without sensors.

00:01:12.106 --> 00:01:18.521
A coverage map should connect use cases to sources and state limitations openly.

00:01:18.521 --> 00:01:23.608
Noisy data creates a different gap between collection and visibility.

00:01:23.608 --> 00:01:30.907
Duplicate alarms, unstable asset names, missing fields, parser errors, and excessive low-value events consume attention.

00:01:30.907 --> 00:01:36.879
Monitor source health, event rate, delay, loss, schema changes, and enrichment success.

00:01:36.879 --> 00:01:39.312
Quality control is continuous.

00:01:39.312 --> 00:01:48.823
Assign source owners, test changes, investigate collection failures, protect integrity, and review whether retained data still supports operations and security.

00:01:48.823 --> 00:01:58.334
A large archive is not a telemetry program unless teams can find, trust, interpret, and act on what it contains.
